<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>4.11.7: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01060</md:content-id>
    <md:title>4.11.7: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>bb54ac74-2064-460c-8dbf-2e230c3f82b7</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section id="sect-00001">
      <para id="para-00001">Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
      <section class="check-understanding" id="sect-00002">
        <exercise id="_548dcd73-d585-4139-a459-d6bf8980d9fe" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00001">
            <para id="para-00002">For questions 1 - 3, use the graph below.</para>
            <para id="para-00003">
                      <media alt="This graph shows four functions on an x, y coordinate plane. The \(x\)-axis runs from negative 8 to 9. The \(y\)-axis runs from negative 8 to 8.  The first shows the decreasing function h of x = negative 2 times x plus 2. It passes through the points (0, 2) and (1, 0). The second is an increasing function that shows f of x = 2 times x plus 3. It passes through the points (0, 3) and (-1.5, 0). The third is an increasing function that shows j of x = 2 times x minus 6 and passes through the points (0, -6) and (3, 0). The fourth line is an increasing function where g of x = x divided by 2 minus 4 and passes through the points (0, -4) and (2 ,0).">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_14_16_01.jpg"/>
                </media>
              
          </para>
            <para id="para-00004">Tell the shift from <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>j</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> to <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
            <para id="para-00005">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00006">Down 3</para>
            <para id="para-00007">Down 8</para>
            <para id="para-00008">Up 9</para>
            <para id="para-00009">Up 8</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00001">
            <para id="para-00010">Correct! Up 9</para>
            <para id="para-00011">Try again. Revisit activity 4.11.2.</para>
            <para id="para-00012">The correct answer is up 9.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_5eae2be9-0274-4a58-9340-3bca315b5440" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00002">
            <para id="para-00013">Tell the transformations from <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> to <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>h</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
            <para id="para-00014">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00015">Vertical reflection, up 1</para>
            <para id="para-00016">Vertical reflection, down 1</para>
            <para id="para-00017">Vertical stretch, right 1</para>
            <para id="para-00018">Vertical stretch, left 1</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00002">
            <para id="para-00019">Correct! Vertical reflection, down 1</para>
            <para id="para-00020">Try again. Revisit activities 4.11.2 – 4.11.4.</para>
            <para id="para-00021">The correct answer is vertical reflection, down 1.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_0086830d-c6d4-4fca-b4c6-9e78332d2635" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00003">
            <para id="para-00022">Describe the transformations made from the parent linear function to achieve <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mfrac><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.
         <emphasis>Select two</emphasis> that apply:
      </para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00003">
            <para id="para-00023">Correct! Vertical compression of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math>; Down 4</para>
            <para id="para-00024">Try again. Revisit activities 4.11.2 – 4.11.4.</para>
            <para id="para-00025">The correct answers are vertical compression of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math>, down 4.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="d22bcd2b-aa35-487b-8ddf-30111943cf25" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00004">
            <para id="para-00026">
                      <media alt="This graph shows two lines on an x, y coordinate plane. The \(x\)-axis runs from negative 4 to 6. The \(y\)-axis runs from negative 3 to 8.  The first line has the equation y = -3 times x divided by 2 plus 1.  The second line has the equation y = -3 times x divided by 2 plus 7.  The lines do not cross.">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_14_16_02.jpg"/>
                </media>
               </para>
              <para id="para-00027">What are the equations of the two lines shown?<emphasis>Select two</emphasis> that apply:</para>
         
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00004">
            <para id="para-00028">Correct! <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mfrac><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mfrac><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00029">Try again. Revisit activity 4.11.1.</para>
            <para id="para-00030">The correct answers are <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mfrac><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mfrac><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_356feacc-af8e-4824-9fa8-1fa282e2d1f4" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00005">
            <para id="para-00031">The linear function <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> has a vertical stretch of 3, a vertical reflection, and a vertical shift down 4. Which of the following is the new function?</para>
            <para id="para-00032">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00033"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00034"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00035"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00036"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00005">
            <para id="para-00037">Correct! <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00038">Try again. Revisit activities 4.11.2 – 4.11.4.</para>
            <para id="para-00039">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_90cae9a1-c577-4ffa-a698-0752ff5525af" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00006">
            <para id="para-00040">The linear function <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> has a vertical compression of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math> and a vertical shift up 2. Which of the following is the new function?</para>
            <para id="para-00041">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00042"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mfrac><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00043"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mfrac><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00044"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00045"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00006">
            <para id="para-00046">Correct! <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mfrac><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00047">Try again. Revisit activities 4.11.2 – 4.11.4.</para>
            <para id="para-00048">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mfrac><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_23cd6648-507a-4211-b236-f0868aca4911" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00007">
            <para id="para-00049">What is the equation of the function graphed? </para>
          <para id="para-00050">(<media alt="This graph shows a linear function graphed on an x y coordinate plane. The x axis is labeled from negative 2 to 8 and the y axis is labeled from negative 1 to 8. The function f is graph along the points (0, 7) and (4, 4)."><image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_14_16_03.jpg"/></media>)</para>
     
            <para id="para-00051">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00052"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00053"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mfrac><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00054"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mfrac><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00055"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mfrac><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00007">
            <para id="para-00056">Correct! <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mfrac><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00057">Try again. Revisit activities 4.11.1 – 4.11.4.</para>
            <para id="para-00058">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mfrac><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="a257dca8-2c02-47e2-bc99-3ccbffc3ed08" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00008">
            <para id="para-00059">The linear function <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> has a vertical compression of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math> and a vertical shift down 2. Which of the following is the new function?</para>
            <para id="para-00060">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00061"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mfrac><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00062"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mfrac><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00063"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00064"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00008">
            <para id="para-00065">Correct! <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mfrac><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00066">Try again. Revisit activities 4.11.2 – 4.11.4.</para>
            <para id="para-00067">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mfrac><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_67af96c8-1a0c-4c07-9b8b-a709e7d55dbb" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00009">
            <para id="para-00068">Which two transformations can be used to obtain the graph of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mi>c</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> from the graph of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
            <para id="para-00069">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00070">A translation to the right <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>c</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> units followed by a reflection across the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-axis</para>
            <para id="para-00071">A translation to the left <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>c</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> units followed by a reflection across the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-axis</para>
            <para id="para-00072">A translation to the right <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>c</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> units followed by a reflection across the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-axis</para>
            <para id="para-00073">A translation to the left <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>c</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> units followed by a reflection across the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-axis</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00009">
            <para id="para-00074">Correct! A translation to the right <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>c</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> units followed by a reflection across the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-axis.</para>
            <para id="para-00075">Try again. Revisit activities 4.11.2 and 4.11.3.</para>
            <para id="para-00076">The correct answer is: A translation to the right <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>c</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> units followed by a reflection across the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-axis.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="a458c908-a4d6-4aaa-8e32-532cf9418259" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00010">
            <para id="para-00077">For the functions <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>h</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, which statement is true if <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>h</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>14</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>12</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
            <para id="para-00078">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00079">The graph of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>h</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is the result of the graph of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> being translated right 14 units and down 12 units.</para>
            <para id="para-00080">The graph of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>h</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is the result of the graph of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> being translated left 14 units and down 12 units.</para>
            <para id="para-00081">The graph of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>h</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is the result of the graph of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> being translated right 14 units and up 12 units.</para>
            <para id="para-00082">The graph of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>h</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is the result of the graph of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> being translated left 14 units and up 12 units.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00010">
            <para id="para-00083">Correct! The graph of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>h</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is the result of the graph of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> being translated left 14 units and down 12 units.</para>
            <para id="para-00084">Try again. Revisit activity 4.11.2.</para>
            <para id="para-00085">The correct answer is: The graph of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>h</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is the result of the graph of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> being translated left 14 units and down 12 units.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_14fc61a9-cead-4fcb-b070-e24a7df09970" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00011">
            <para id="para-00086">Which type of transformation can be used to obtain the graph of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> from the graph of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
            <para id="para-00087">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00088">Vertical shrink or compression</para>
            <para id="para-00089">Vertical shift down</para>
            <para id="para-00090">Vertical shift up</para>
            <para id="para-00091">Vertical stretch</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00011">
            <para id="para-00092">Correct! The correct transformation is a vertical stretch.</para>
            <para id="para-00093">Try again. Revisit activity 4.11.3.</para>
            <para id="para-00094">The correct answer is: vertical stretch.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
    </section>
